fies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le09ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About Events in the Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Events that happen in your life are called life events. Life events are usually important to remember.<br> You use expressions like <span class=\"italic\"> life-changing</span> or <span class=\"italic\">Did you know that \u2026 ?</span>  to describe key life events.<br><br>You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished event or a specific time in the past.<br><br>You can form the regular form of the Simple Past tense by adding <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"strong\">-ied</span> to the verb.<br><br>Some verbs are irregular. Their Past Simple form doesn't end in <span class=\"strong\"> -ed</span> or<span class=\"strong\"> -ied</span>, like <span class=\"italic\">came</span> or <span class=\"italic\">was</span> or <span class=\"italic\">won</span>.<br><br>You use wh-questions to ask about past events."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: When was the first time you went on a boat race?<br> <span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: I participated in the Belize River Challenge. It was a life-changing experience."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About Events in the Present"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Simple Present tense to talk about a routine or a specific action that happens regularly.<br><br>You can use expressions of frequency like <span class=\"italic\">every day</span> or <span class=\"italic\">always</span> with the Simple Present.<br><br>You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about an action happening right now. You can also use the Present Continuous to talk about events that <span class=\"strong\">are happening</span> soon.  You make the Present Continuous with the verb <span class=\"strong\">to be + -ing</span>.<br><br>You use wh-questions to ask about life events in the present."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Simple\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The race commemorates the Maya tradition. <br><br> Sally travels every month for work.<br><br>  Peter spends a lot of time in the office.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">People are commemorating the Maya heritage  today. <br><br> Sally is traveling through Europe right now. <br><br> Vanessa is spending the summer in San Francisco.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: Where are you traveling to next?<br> <span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: I'm leaving for Mexico tomorrow."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "handmade "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "made by hand not machine "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can buy handmade goods at the market."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words to review!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tourist season"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a popular time of the year for tourists "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: July is our tourist season."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to grow tired of "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to become bored with something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I grew tired of London and its gray skies"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "remarkable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "important; easy to remember"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Mayan culture is remarkable."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "legacy "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something received from past generations"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The River Challenge celebrates the Mayan legacy in Belize."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to commemorate "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to celebrate; to honor "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The race commemorates the Maya tradition."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "civilization"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the culture and history or a group of people "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Mayan civilization was fascinating."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob11aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "life-changing"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very important; an event that changes your life "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The River Challenge was a life-changing experience."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob11aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "memorable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something you remember for a long time "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The trip was memorable!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob11aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "I'm having the time of my life! "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "I'm having a lot of fun! "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Belize River Challenge is exciting. I'm having the time of my life!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le09ob11aud10"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write an interview with your partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Think of a life-changing event or make one up."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask 4-5 questions about the event. Use <span class=\"italic\">wh-</span> questions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the dialogue aloud with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Switch roles with your partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I do an interview."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask personal questions about a past life event."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I answer questions as the interviewee."}]}], "type": "sena"}